# HIVE_MODEL=glm HIVE_VRAM_GB=96 — start values from docs/vram-footprint.md (§2 lean set, §3.1 per card); the sweep refines them.
# Shipped configuration of the family fits this card (docs/vram-footprint.md §3.1); the measured overrides follow. HIVE_VRAM_LIMIT_MB is derived
#   from HIVE_VRAM_GB (none for 96 = the whole card); the expert cache fills what is left (HIVE_CACHE_FIT).
# 5 layer-major blocks of 16,384 rows (81,920 per call) so the 64K bench prompt (67,510 rows) runs in one
#   pass instead of 65,536 + 1,974 rows (the short second pass streamed most non-resident experts again), and HIVE_GLM_PREFILL_ROWBLOCK=16384
#   to bound the per-expert prefill scratch. Decode unchanged (prefill-only switches). Short benchmark pass (warm c4, max_tokens 150, c1/c4/c8, 64K,
#   image after): c4/c8 83.9/108.4 → 83.9/109.0 tok/s · 64K TTFT 19.92 → 15.74 s · peak 94,696 of 97,887 MiB used. glm_check at 96 GB
#   (reference prompts): top-1 match and greedy prefixes within the run-to-run spread of the previous build.
HIVE_GLM_PREFILL_TILES=5
HIVE_GLM_PREFILL_ROWBLOCK=16384
